# STIG CD16-00-006900: PostgreSQL Security Definer Functions
# STIG ID: V-261916 (MEDIUM) - Elevated privilege execution must be restricted
# Check: SELECT from pg_proc -> no SECURITY DEFINER functions outside system schemas
# Finding: User-defined security definer function detected

META
    esp_id `pg16-cd16-00-006900-security-definer-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `pg16`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG CD16-00-006900: PostgreSQL Security Definer Functions`
    description `Validates that no user-defined functions use SECURITY DEFINER outside of system schemas. Security definer functions execute with the privileges of the function owner rather than the calling user, creating a privilege escalation path if misused.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `pg16,stig,security-definer,privilege-escalation,ac-6,disa-stig`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:CD16-00-006900,NIST-800-53:AC-6(8)`
    control_objective `AC-6(8)`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `dba`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `PostgreSQL16:localhost:pg-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review all SECURITY DEFINER functions outside pg_catalog and information_schema. Remove the SECURITY DEFINER attribute or move the function to a system schema if the elevated privilege is justified.`

    component_id `comp-pg16-db`

    impl_AC_6_8 `PostgreSQL implements privilege level controls for code execution by restricting the use of SECURITY DEFINER functions to system schemas only. The pg_proc catalog is queried to identify any user-defined functions that execute with the privileges of the function owner rather than the invoker. Functions outside pg_catalog and information_schema with the SECURITY DEFINER attribute represent unauthorized privilege escalation paths that bypass role-based access controls.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT pg_secdef_check
        query `security_definer_functions`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE no_user_secdef
        row_count int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN pg_catalog_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF no_user_secdef
            OBJECT_REF pg_secdef_check
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
